% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for garments and fabrics, in the words of the tariff.
% Each word cites the text that says what it means: US Customs' publication
% on apparel terminology, the tariff's notes, US Customs rulings. Bridges.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* is made of the fabric *a name*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a name* is a word for the residual kind *a kind*.
    *a good* is named by a specific kind.
    *a field* is a field that names the kind.
    *a field* is a field that names the fabric.
    *a name* is a fabric of construction *a construction*.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the knowledge base garments background includes:

the apparel terminology publication is published at "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/rulings/informed-compliance-publications".
the text of the apparel terminology publication is at "../sources/cbp_icp/apparel_terminology.txt".
the listing format is published at "https://huggingface.co/datasets/ATH-MaaS/HSCodeComp".
the text of the listing format is at "../sources/listings/marketplace_fields.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 61 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2061".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 61 is at "../sources/hts/chapter_61.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 62 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2062".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 62 is at "../sources/hts/chapter_62.txt".
ruling NY N315788 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N315788".
the text of ruling NY N315788 is at "../sources/cbp/N315788.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 52 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2052".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 52 is at "../sources/hts/chapter_52.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 54 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2054".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 54 is at "../sources/hts/chapter_54.txt".
ruling NY N319174 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N319174".
the text of ruling NY N319174 is at "../sources/cbp/N319174.txt".
ruling NY N352158 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N352158".
the text of ruling NY N352158 is at "../sources/cbp/N352158.txt".

% The fields of a listing that name what the product is
"item type" is a field that names the kind,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words".
"tops type" is a field that names the kind,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Tops Type (13 listings): the kind of top".
"fabric type" is a field that names the fabric,
    as stated in the listing format, confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric".

% Garment words (US Customs, Apparel Terminology under the HTSUS, 2008)
"t-shirt" is a word for the kind T-shirt,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "T-shirts (6109, 6111) - are underwear style garments".
"t-shirts" is a word for the kind T-shirt,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "T-shirts (6109, 6111) - are underwear style garments".
"tank top" is a word for the kind tank top,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Tank tops (6109) - are sleeveless garments with oversized armholes".
"tank tops" is a word for the kind tank top,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Tank tops (6109) - are sleeveless garments with oversized armholes".
% "top" is the word for what no more specific word names
"top" is a word for the residual kind top,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113".
"tops" is a word for the residual kind top,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113".
"sweater" is a word for the kind sweater,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Sweaters (6110, 6111) - are knit garments".
"sweaters" is a word for the kind sweater,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Sweaters (6110, 6111) - are knit garments".
"pullover" is a word for the kind pullover,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Pullovers (6110, 6111) - are upper body knit garments".
"sweatshirt" is a word for the kind sweatshirt,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Sweatshirts (6110, 6111) - are pullover style garments".
"hoodie" is a word for the kind pullover,
    as stated in ruling NY N319174, confer "Hoodie is a pullover".
"dresses" is a word for the kind dress,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Dresses (6104, 6111, 6204, 6209) - are one-piece garments for women or girls".
"prom dresses" is a word for the kind dress,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Dresses (6104, 6111, 6204, 6209) - are one-piece garments for women or girls".
"trousers" is a word for the kind trousers,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Trousers (6103, 6104, 6111, 6203, 6204, 6209, 6210) - are outerwear garments with leg separations extending below the knee".
"pants" is a word for the kind trousers,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Trousers (6103, 6104, 6111, 6203, 6204, 6209, 6210) - are outerwear garments with leg separations extending below the knee".
"shorts" is a word for the kind shorts,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Shorts (6103, 6104, 6203, 6204) - are trousers which do not cover the knee or below".
"briefs" is a word for the kind briefs,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Briefs (6107, 6108, 6207, 6208, 6210) - are tight fitting short underpants".
"panties" is a word for the kind panties,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Panties (6108, 6208) - are women's and girl's short underpants".
"bodysuit" is a word for the kind bodysuit,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Bodysuits and bodyshirts (6114) - are knit one-piece garments".
"swimwear" is a word for the kind swimsuit,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Swimwear (6112, 6211) - is a term referring to garments designed for swimming".
"tights" is a word for the kind tights,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Tights (6115) - are form-fitting hosiery, covering the waist and leg".
"gloves" is a word for the kind gloves,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Gloves (6116, 6216) - are".
"brassiere" is a word for the kind brassiere,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Brassieres (6212) - are garments worn to mold and/or support the breasts".
"vest" is a word for the kind vest,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Vests (6110, 6211) - are upper body garments resembling a sleeveless sweater or jacket".

% Fabric words: the tariff's own definitions, and US Customs rulings
"jersey" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric".
"interlock" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric".
"rib" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in ruling NY N352158, confer "rib knit fabric for the neckband".
"broadcloth" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "The term \"poplin or broadcloth\" means plain weave fabrics".
"poplin" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "The term \"poplin or broadcloth\" means plain weave fabrics".
"denim" is a fabric of construction woven,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 52, confer "the expression \"denim\" means fabrics of yarns of different colors".


% Added after the diagnostic of FactsBackground.md §5.3 (step 6): words the
% listings used that the background did not know, each found in a text.
"dress" is a word for the kind dress,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "dresses, skirts, divided skirts, trousers".
"skirt" is a word for the kind skirt,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "dresses, skirts, divided skirts, trousers".
"skirts" is a word for the kind skirt,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "dresses, skirts, divided skirts, trousers".
"shirts" is a word for the kind shirt,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "“Shirts” and “shirt-blouses” are garments designed to cover the upper part of the body".
"blouses" is a word for the kind blouse,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "“Shirts” and “shirt-blouses” are garments designed to cover the upper part of the body".
"pajamas" is a word for the kind pajamas,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' underpants, briefs, nightshirts, pajamas".
"robe" is a word for the kind bathrobe,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles".
"robes" is a word for the kind bathrobe,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles".
"dressing gown" is a word for the kind dressing gown,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles".
"jumpsuit" is a word for the kind jumpsuit,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Coveralls, jumpsuits and similar apparel".
"brassieres" is a word for the kind brassiere,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Brassieres, girdles, corsets, braces, suspenders, garters".
"camisole" is a word for the kind top,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Camisoles are garments that provide limited shoulder coverage".
"romper" is a word for the kind romper,
    as stated in ruling NY N315788, confer "is a woman’s romper constructed from 100% viscose woven fabric".
"rompers" is a word for the kind romper,
    as stated in ruling NY N315788, confer "is a woman’s romper constructed from 100% viscose woven fabric".
"knitted" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "ARTICLES OF APPAREL AND CLOTHING ACCESSORIES, KNITTED OR CROCHETED".

rule kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Apparel Terminology under the HTSUS":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind the kind.

rule kind_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the value is a word for the kind the kind.

rule specific_kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
a good is named by a specific kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind a kind.

rule specific_kind_by_field with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
a good is named by a specific kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for the kind a kind.

rule residual_kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the residual kind the kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by a specific kind.

rule residual_kind_by_field with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for the residual kind the kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by a specific kind.

rule construction_by_fabric with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the garment is made of the fabric a name
    and the name is a fabric of construction the construction.

rule construction_by_fabric_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the fabric
    and the name is a fabric of construction the construction.

scenario tee is:
    tee is called "t-shirt".
    tee is made of the fabric "jersey".
    hood is called "hoodie".
    the field "fabric type" of blouse reads "broadcloth".
    the field "item type" of skirt one reads "tops".
    the field "tops type" of tee reads "tops".
    kinds expects answers ["the kind of tee is T-shirt", "the kind of hood is pullover", "the kind of skirt one is top"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of tee is knitted", "the fabric construction of blouse is woven"].

query kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.
